module Core

### Runs one cycle-collection pass for {Roamed[T]} entities and frees what is provably cyclic garbage: a Bacon-Rajan
### synchronous recycler (trial deletion) that reclaims the cycles reference counting alone leaks. The collector is
### Ingrid's (`Ingrid/tessera/cycle.tess`), shared with Suflae: every strong release that leaves a count above zero
### reports the entity there, and a pass stops the world, finds the candidates reachable only from each other, and
### frees them through each type's free hook.
### :returns: How many entities this pass freed. 0 means nothing was collected.
routine cyclic_collect() -> U64
    danger
        return C::ingrid_cyclic_collect()

### Universal cycle-collector visit hook. Only a `Roamed[T]` handle owns a strong edge the collector
### must follow — every OTHER type (values, plain records, container buffers of values) participates in
### no cycle, so the default is a no-op. `Roamed[T].cyclic_visit` (in Roamed.rf) is the hand-written
### override that actually reports the controller. This universal default lets a generic container
### buffer-walk call `element.cyclic_visit()` uniformly: a value element compiles to nothing, a
### `Roamed` element reports itself — no per-element-type branching in the builder/codegen.
@overridable
dangerous routine T.cyclic_visit()
needs AnyType T
    return
